PURPOSE of /kernel/wireless_tests/functional/suspend_resume
Decription: Test to ensure wireless connections are maintained across
            suspend/resume.
Author: Ken Benoit <kbenoit@redhat.com>

0.Purpose
=========
This is a basic wireless connection test that also performs a suspend and resume
of the test system. This is meant to ensure that a system can be resumed and
that the wireless connection can be re-established without user intervention.

1.Files
=======
Makefile - used to run the test script.
runtest.sh - script that starts the wireless connection creation, calls the
             Python script perform the suspend/resume, and then delete the
             wireless connection.
PURPOSE - this file
test.py - Python script that performs the actual suspend/resume.
__init__.py - used for Python module pathing.

2.Process
=========
Simply run the following command:
# make run

3.Test params
=============
This /distribution/setup_repository test accepts the following parameters in the
XML:

(OPTIONAL)
PRESET - Preset defined in the preconfigured_setups.json file provided with
         /kernel/wireless_tests/functional/connection/setup.

3.Example xml snippet
=====================
<task name="/kernel/wireless_tests/functional/suspend_resume" role="STANDALONE">
    <params>
        <param name="PRESET" value="unencrypted"/>
    </params>
</task>

=================
-end PURPOSE file
